findings.body:
The diff deletes `ghost/i18n/locales/zh/comments.json` (all 72 translations). The PR description says the opposite: it says the file was *refined* ("consistent 评论/名字 terms and clearer load/show hints").

Nothing will fail loudly. `generateResources` catches the failed `require` and loads the English file instead:

::code{file="ghost/i18n/lib/i18n.js" lines="13-22"}

So every Ghost site set to `zh` would show the comments widget in English ("Add comment", "Load more", "Sign in"…). The `zh-Hant` locale still has its comments.json, which makes this look like a mistake rather than a deliberate choice.

::callout{type="warning"}
This is a user-facing regression that the description doesn't mention. Restore the file, then apply the intended wording changes (评论/名字, load/show hints) as edits to it.

The edits in ghost.json are a reasonable reference for the intended wording, e.g. "Name" → 名字:

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/ghost.json" lines="27-31"}

The new translation removes the `{newsletterName}` variable:

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="9-9"}

Portal passes the newsletter's name in bold to this string in `apps/portal/src/components/pages/account-email-page.js:70-73` and `unsubscribe-page.js:244-247`. Without the placeholder, a Chinese reader who unsubscribes from one newsletter on a site with several just sees "you will no longer receive newsletters". That reads as though they've unsubscribed from *everything*, and it no longer matches what the sibling string `{memberEmail} will no longer receive this newsletter.` says.

The `ghost/i18n/no-unused-variables` rule in `ghost/i18n/test/i18n.lint.js` exists to catch exactly this.

::suggestion{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="9-9"}
    "{memberEmail} will no longer receive {newsletterName} newsletter.": "{memberEmail}将不会再收到{newsletterName}的新闻信。",

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="116-117"}

`t('Name')` labels the member's personal name input in `signup-page.js:529`, `account-profile-page.js:138` and `offer-page.js:209`. In mainland usage, 名称 is for the name of an organization, product or object. A person's name is 姓名 or 名字. The old value 名字 was already correct, and this PR sets ghost.json to 名字 too, so this edit leaves the two files inconsistent.

::suggestion{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="117-117"}
    "Name": "名字",

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="212-213"}

This string is a status label in `AccountHomePage/components/email-preferences-action.js:11`, shown when the member's email is currently disabled (spam complaint or bounce). 您将不会收到邮件 means "you will not receive emails", which sounds like a future consequence rather than the current state. The line just above it, `You're currently not receiving emails`, uses the present-tense 您当前不会收到邮件. Something like 您目前收不到邮件 describes the state more accurately.

::suggestion{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="213-213"}
    "You're not receiving emails": "您目前收不到邮件。",
